From bafce31f92c0486d4d6cc48887d1044b88fa3483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:55:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Server: one ESBT room per document; Loro and
 Hocuspocus/Yjs removed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EsbtRoom keeps the loro-room shape — full server replica, version-vector
delta on join, debounced persist, idle eviction, discard-on-delete — with
a stable per-document site id (marks-server:<id>) so a restart resumes the
same replica instead of bloating every client's reconnect vector (§6).
The upgrade path accepts only /collab/esbt/:id; the retired loro and yjs
paths and rows created by those engines are refused so a stale client
cannot corrupt stored state. Legacy rows stay listed but export empty.
Seed and export go through EsbtDoc. loro-crdt, yjs and both Hocuspocus
packages leave the dependency tree.
